---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, ACCOUNTS, ACCOUNTS_ENABLED } from '../config/site';

const title = 'Privacy | AuditYourHome';
const description = 'What AuditYourHome collects, why, where it is stored, who sees it, and how to download or delete it. Plain language, updated October 20, 2026.';
const updated = 'October 20, 2026';
const address = ACCOUNTS.mailingAddress || 'Wakefield, Quebec';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy, plainly</h1>
      <p class="lede">What we collect, why, where it’s kept, who sees it, and how to get it back or delete it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="measure prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        AuditYourHome is operated by Click Shift Marketing, {address}. The person in charge of protecting
        personal information is Dave Bussell, owner: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        Write to him for any question, request or complaint about your information.
      </p>

      <h2>The planner and calculators</h2>
      <p>
        The Home Energy Planner and the calculators run in your browser. Postal codes, bills and answers you
        enter are worked out on your device and aren’t sent to us{ACCOUNTS_ENABLED ? ', unless you choose to save your plan to a free account or ask to be matched' : ''}.
        They appear in the page’s address only if you use “copy link”, so you control sharing.
      </p>

      {ACCOUNTS_ENABLED ? (
        <Fragment>
          <h2>Free accounts (My Home)</h2>
          <p>
            If you create an account we keep: your email address; your name and phone number if you add them;
            the home details, audit and test records, upgrade plan and reminders you enter; your alert choices
            with the wording and time of your consent; and any match requests. We use them only to run your
            account, send the alerts you chose and handle the requests you make.
          </p>
          <p>
            Signing in uses a code or link sent to your email: we never store a password. Your account data is
            stored with Supabase in its Canada (Central) region, in Montréal. Database rules let only you read
            and change your own records.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our admins (Dave and anyone he designates to arrange matches) can see match requests and, for people
            who ask to be matched, the home details and records needed to find the right company. They can’t see
            the homes of people who never asked for a match.
          </p>

          <h2>Match requests</h2>
          <p>
            When you ask to be matched, and tick the box to agree, we share your request, contact details and
            home details with one company that serves your area, so it can contact you about that request. We
            never share it with more than one company per request and never sell contact lists. Participating
            companies pay us a referral fee; you pay nothing, and it never affects the directory. We confirm your
            email address with a code first; a request that isn’t confirmed within 7 days is deleted.
          </p>

          <h2>Email alerts</h2>
          <p>
            Alerts are off until you turn them on, and you choose which ones: rebate and program changes for your
            provinces, reminders before dates you add, and a monthly home checklist. Every alert says who it’s from
            and has a one-click unsubscribe link that works without signing in; you can also change alerts in My Home.
            We also email you about requests you make, such as when you’ve been matched.
          </p>
          <p>
            Emails, including sign-in codes, are sent through Resend, an email delivery service that processes
            your email address and the message in the United States. We send it only what’s needed to deliver
            each email.
          </p>
        </Fragment>
      ) : (
        <Fragment>
          <h2>Requests and questions</h2>
          <p>
            If you send us a request through a form on this site, or by email, to be matched, we use your details to
            connect you with one registered service organization or contractor serving your area, and for no other
            purpose. Participating companies pay us a referral fee for these introductions; you pay nothing. We don’t
            sell contact lists, and we never share your request with more than one company. US questions are only
            answered by email; we don’t pass them to anyone.
          </p>
          <p>
            Forms are handled by Netlify, the company that hosts this site. It stores what you submit in the United
            States and emails it to us, and we keep it only as long as we need to deal with your request. If you email
            us, we have your email address; we use it to reply.
          </p>
        </Fragment>
      )}

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        On public pages we use Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to see which pages are useful and where
        people get stuck. They set cookies and record how pages are used; Clarity can replay a visit, with what
        you type in our forms hidden. Neither runs on account pages{ACCOUNTS_ENABLED ? ' (My Home, the admin console and the unsubscribe page)' : ''}.
        You can block them with your browser’s privacy settings or an ad blocker; the site works the same.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what we hold about you, correct it, get a copy in a common format, or have it deleted.
        {ACCOUNTS_ENABLED && ' In My Home you can do most of this yourself: edit anything, download all your data as a file, or delete your account and everything attached to it at once.'}
        You can withdraw consent at any time. If you’re not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to
        Quebec’s <a href="https://www.cai.gouv.qc.ca/" rel="noopener">Commission d’accès à l’information</a> or the
        <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/" rel="noopener">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        {ACCOUNTS_ENABLED
          ? 'Account information stays until you delete your account or ask us to. Deleting your account removes your home details, records, plan, reminders, alert settings and match requests. Unconfirmed requests are deleted after 7 days. Emails you send us are kept as long as needed to deal with them.'
          : 'Emails you send us are kept as long as needed to deal with them.'}
      </p>

      <p class="small">
        If we change how we handle personal information, we’ll update this page and the date at the top.
        Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .prose { padding-bottom: 56px; }
</style>
